    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47642&jobTitle=Access+and+Inclusive+Design+Specialist": {
      "title": "Access and Inclusive Design Specialist",
      "description": "Job details: Access and Inclusive Design Specialist Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Access and Inclusive Design Specialist Apply Now Ref Number B28-00353 Professional Expertise Estates, Facilities, Accommodation and Safety Department Finance, Commercial and Estates (B28) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £43,981-£54,019​ Contract Type Permanent Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment No Closing Date 10-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About us UCL is one of the world’s leading universities, home to a diverse and growing community of students, staff, and partners. Our estate spans more than 230 buildings across London and is evolving rapidly, including the development of our new UCL East campus on the Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park. As we expand, we are committed to creating environments that are accessible, inclusive, healthy, and welcoming to all. Improving the accessibility of our estate is a central priority, and we are investing in the expertise and innovation needed to ensure our spaces reflect the values of openness, equity, and excellence that define UCL. About the role As an Access & Inclusive Design Specialist, you will play a key role in shaping an inclusive campus by providing expert client‑side advice across UCL’s estate projects and facilities services. Working within the Sustainability Team and supporting the Head of Inclusive Environments, you will help embed inclusive design principles into project processes, undertake access audits, and guide teams in addressing accessibility challenges across a complex and historic estate. Your work will directly contribute to UCL’s long‑term Inclusive Environments Action Plan, ensuring our buildings, spaces, and operations support healthy, productive, and equitable experiences for all who use them. About you You are an experienced and knowledgeable inclusive design professional who brings both technical expertise and a passion for creating environments that work for everyone. You understand the complexities of accessibility across a varied estate and can confidently apply current and emerging inclusive design standards to new builds, refurbishments, heritage buildings, and public realm projects. You thrive in collaborative settings, working effectively with a wide range of stakeholders, and you bring creativity, initiative, and strong communication skills to every challenge. Above all, you are motivated by the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the lived experience of UCL’s diverse community. What we offer As well as exciting opportunities, UCL offers a range of great benefits. Find out more: UCL Rewards and Benefits . 41 days’ holiday (27 days annual leave, 8 bank holidays, 6 closure days) Option to purchase 5 additional days’ annual leave Defined benefit career average revalued earnings pension scheme (CARE) Cycle to work scheme, season ticket loan, and immigration loan Relocation support for eligible posts On-site nursery and gym Enhanced maternity, paternity, and adoption pay Staff Support Service (employee assistance programme) Discounted medical insurance Full details: UCL Rewards and Benefits . Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation. We are committed to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to being a place where we all belong. We particularly encourage applications from candidates underrepresented in UCL’s workforce, including those from Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds, disabled people, and – for Grade 9 and 10 roles – women.” Read more: UCL Equality, Diversity and Inclusion . Applicants should also familiarise themselves with UCL’s policies on: Prevention of Bullying, Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy and Personal Relationships Policy Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: 2022nov21 Access and Inclusive Design Specialist JD.docx arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
