    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47327&jobTitle=Agile+Delivery+Manager": {
      "title": "Agile Delivery Manager",
      "description": "Job details: Agile Delivery Manager Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Agile Delivery Manager Apply Now Ref Number B01-05657 Professional Expertise IT and Digital Department Vice-President (Operations) (B01) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £56,431-£66,437​ Contract Type Permanent Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment No Closing Date 07-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About us Information Services Division (ISD) is the primary provider of IT services to UCL.  We support and enhance learning, teaching, research and administrative processes by providing information- and technology-related services to over 50,000 staff and students of UCL and associated institutions. Our ambition is to be the leading IT services group in the Higher Education (HE) sector, and we are growing our team’s capability in experience/UX, agile development, security, cloud, service management and partnering. We are modernising our technology foundations, digitising the processes of the university to transform experience for students and staff, and partnering across the university to drive differentiation in UCL education and research. UCL boasts a track record of ground-breaking research that transforms the lives of people around the world. Our teams provide dedicated, specialist support throughout the research and innovation lifecycle to help sustain and advance UCL’s position as a world-class, research-led university. The Centre for Advanced Research Computing (ARC) is UCL’s institute for infrastructure and innovation in digital research – the supercomputers, datasets, software and people that make computational science and digital scholarship possible. ARC is UCL’s research, innovation and service centre for the tools, practices and systems that enable computational science and digital scholarship. ARC’s role is to: Provide advanced, reliable and secure digital research infrastructure to research groups in UCL and beyond and; Act as a laboratory for research, teaching and innovation in compute, data and software intensive research methods. About the role As an Agile Delivery Manager (ADM) you will support, coach, and lead teams within the Advanced Research Computing change portfolio to deliver the services and systems which make data and compute-intensive research possible, facilitating meaningful change for UCL’s research community. In this role, you will be working alongside Research Software Engineers and Infrastructure Developers to deliver UCL’s private cloud and secure data environments. This role requires excellent stakeholder and communication skills, and to operate with credibility in a busy operational environment. A proven ability to deliver Projects/Epics/Features end-to-end in a complex environment is essential, as is the ability to adopt agile approaches to delivery (with support). Business change management experience will also be useful in this role, as you will have the opportunity to guide UCL researchers through change as we transform our service delivery approach. You will lead and facilitate stakeholder engagement, Project/Epic/Feature delivery and collaborative Agile ceremonies, motivating team members and wider stakeholders to achieve key outcomes. In this role, you will anticipate and mitigate risks, manage issues and dependencies, and remove blockers and impediments, fostering a ‘can do’ attitude and bringing clarity and purpose to delivery. You will also lead your Product Team during Termly Increment (TI) Planning, as well as reporting on progress during termly ‘Inspect & Adapt’ and Vision sessions. You will work closely with other delivery managers, capability leads and ARC and ISD leadership, establishing and maintaining strong working relationships to deliver complex projects set out in UCL’s Digital Strategic Plan. You'll proactively communicate and collaborate with key stakeholders across the change portfolios and the UCL research community. About you As an experienced Agile Delivery or Project Manager, you have experience in delivering projects, with excellent facilitation, collaboration and communication skills. Your interpersonal skills (including the ability to persuade and influence stakeholders) are exceptional and you're naturally curious, always being proactive and looking to continuously improve how you and your team operate. You will need excellent analytical and reporting skills, and a strong ability to work with financial information. You will be able to quickly build an understanding of research and innovation operations and be able to get things done in a busy environment with conflicting priorities. You will be adept at building relationships, leading delivery teams and enjoy a challenge, including scoping and business casing for strategic priorities. You will enjoy the opportunity to develop your skills and work with peers, and you line manager to find creative solutions to challenges. You have also had experience creating and driving business change initiatives. You can use Jira, Teams, Miro and other collaboration tools, and are confident with the budgeting and financial management of your team, always seeking to achieve value for money and benefits realisation. You manage risks and issues proactively, seeking to mitigate risk wherever possible, and manage interdependencies across the ISD portfolios and wider-UCL. Additionally, you have the confidence to represent your team and speak publicly, including leading Agile ceremonies, giving demos, and providing requested information and presentations to senior leadership. You must have proven project management and delivery experience and a relevant qualification. Most of all, you will be committed to delivery of outcomes and benefits to the community and inspire those around you to do the same. What we offer As well as the exciting opportunities this role presents, we also offer some great benefits some of which are below: 41 Days holiday (27 days annual leave 8 bank holiday and 6 closure days) Additional 5 days’ annual leave purchase scheme Defined benefit career average revalued earnings pension scheme (CARE) Cycle to work scheme and season ticket loan Immigration loan Relocation scheme for certain posts On-Site nursery On-site gym Enhanced maternity, paternity and adoption pay Employee assistance programme: Staff Support Service Discounted medical insurance Visit https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/reward-and-benefits to find out more. Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation, and we wantour community to represent the diversity of the world’s talent. We arecommitted to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to beinga place where we all belong. We therefore particularly encourage applications from candidates who are likely to beunderrepresented in UCL’s workforce. These include peoplefrom Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds; disabled people; LGBTQI+people, and for our Grade 9 and 10 roles, women. Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: JD326 ITPPD - Agile Delivery Manager (2).pdf arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
    },
    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47756&jobTitle=Area+Facilities+Manager+": {
      "title": "Area Facilities Manager",
      "description": "Job details: Area Facilities Manager Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Area Facilities Manager Apply Now Ref Number B28-00344 Professional Expertise Estates, Facilities, Accommodation and Safety Department Finance, Commercial and Estates (B28) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £56,431-£66,437​ Contract Type Permanent Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment No Closing Date 16-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About us The UCL Estate comprises over 270 buildings valued at over £3 Billion, more than four million square feet of academic accommodation and approaching 4,250 student bedrooms. The scale, variety and complexity of the Estate are unparalleled in the Higher Education sector The Area Facilities Management Team (AFM Team) is part of the Campus Experience and Infrastructure Division. The AFM Team enables and facilitates the smooth running of the Estate and enhances the customer experience by overseeing campus operations. The buildings supported by the AFM Team are split across five geographical areas, each managed by an Area Facilities Manager (AFM). Reporting into each AFM are Facilities Managers each assigned their own group of buildings to manage. About the role Develop a detailed understanding of all activities within an allocated area to support customers and colleagues in the smooth operational management of the estate. Line management responsibility for Facilities Manager(s) and Facilities Assistant(s) including recruitment, appraisals and development. Build and maintain strong trusted relationships with relevant Department Managers and Heads of Department and liaise with Directors of Operations as required. Act as a point of escalation, coordinating responses to complaints and incidents. Advise on and influence planned works or activities that are not within a single building assigned to a specific Facilities Manager. Duties and Responsibilities Provide cover for Facilities Manager(s) during periods of absence. Analyze data from inspections and other sources to identify trends and compile reports to present at committees and meetings as required. Oversee work for the allocated area, managing Facilities Managers and planning and prioritising works as required. Consolidate feedback from Facilities Managers related to campus operations and provide feedback to senior managers. To directly lead, manage and track actions on escalated matters within the area, working with CE&I teams and landlords to resolve issues and enacting a comms plan as necessary. Work closely with colleagues and customers to identify opportunities to improve services and facilities. Manage a delegated budget for specific works to enhance the customer experience, including the initiation of projects. Represent CE&I or AFM Team at working groups and committees as required, including critical incident response groups. Chair or attend Building User Group (BUG) meetings and schedule site walkrounds with key customers. Oversee completion of site inspections, resolution of safety issues and investigations by Facilities Managers, assisting and/or escalating where necessary. Work collaboratively with stakeholders to resolve escalated issues related to implementation of reasonable adjustments. Engage with the Landlord, Property and other CE&I teams to ensure lease responsibilities are fulfilled where necessary. Act as key contact for Landlord’s operational teams to escalate service provision issues, and review and co-ordinate proposed project works. About you You will bring substantial practical experience of managing or overseeing estates and facilities services within a large, complex organisation, with a strong understanding of health and safety legislation and its application in an operational environment. You will have experience of working with contractors and in-house teams, and of balancing competing priorities in a fast-paced setting. An experienced people manager, you will be confident leading, supporting and developing staff, and comfortable taking accountability for performance, decision-making and outcomes. You will have a collaborative leadership style and be able to build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, influencing effectively and communicating clearly even in pressured or ambiguous situations. You will be confident using IT systems to support and oversee facilities operations, including helpdesk or integrated workplace management systems, and will be comfortable using data to inform decisions and report on performance. Experience of working within higher education or a similarly complex estate would be advantageous, as would familiarity with service specifications, contracts or SLAs. You will be motivated by delivering high-quality services, improving the campus experience and working inclusively with colleagues, students and partners. Above all, you will bring sound judgement, resilience and a proactive approach to solving complex operational challenges. What we offer As well as exciting opportunities, UCL offers a range of great benefits. Find out more: Option to purchase 5 additional days’ annual leave Defined benefit career average revalued earnings pension scheme (CARE) Cycle to work scheme, season ticket loan, and immigration loan Relocation support for eligible posts On-site nursery and gym Enhanced maternity, paternity, and adoption pay Staff Support Service (employee assistance programme) Discounted medical insurance Full details: UCL Rewards and Benefits . Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation. We are committed to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to being a place where we all belong. We particularly encourage applications from candidates underrepresented in UCL’s workforce, including those from Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds, disabled people, and – for Grade 9 and 10 roles – women. Read more: UCL Equality, Diversity and Inclusion . Applicants should also familiarise themselves with UCL’s policies on: Prevention of Bullying, Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy and Personal Relationships Policy Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: Area Facilities Manager.docx arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
    },
    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47648&jobTitle=Assistant+Research+Data+Steward": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Data Steward",
      "description": "Job details: Assistant Research Data Steward Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Assistant Research Data Steward Apply Now Ref Number B01-05628 Professional Expertise IT and Digital Department Vice-President (Operations) (B01) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £36,433-£41,833 Contract Type Permanent Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment No Closing Date 13-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About us The UCL Centre for Advanced Research Computing (ARC) is UCL’s new institute for infrastructure and innovation in digital research - the supercomputers, datasets, software and people that make computational science and digital scholarship possible. We are an innovative hybrid: a professional services department that delivers reliable and secure infrastructure and services to UCL research groups, and a laboratory for research and innovation in the application of advanced computational and data intensive research methods, working in partnership with academics from all fields. We are a home for the research technology professionals - research software engineers, HPC systems engineers, dev-ops specialists, data engineers, data scientists and data stewards - who support and collaborate in the delivery of UCL research. About the role Our Research Data Stewards provide data-focused support and consultancy to researchers at UCL, helping researchers to improve their data management, align with university and funder policies, and enable Open Science and FAIR data. Research Data Stewards also perform independent research into the practice of data and compute intensive research methods. They will spend much of their time embedded within research projects but also contribute to new research proposals and collaborate on research data service design, feeding in researcher requirements to ensure that the suite of research support services offered by UCL remains relevant and effective. This is a Hybrid working role. Salary range for the Assistant Research Data Steward: £36,433 to £42,891 (including London Allowance) depending on experience. Job description and person specification for the Assistant Research Data Steward position can be accessed at the bottom of this page. Please supply a cover letter setting out how you meet the selection criteria. About you As a Research Data Steward, you’ll bring knowledge of conducting or supporting data intensive‑research. You will be committed to producing reliable, sustainable and trustworthy research data and will have experience analysing and solving complex problems. We’re looking for someone who enjoys communicating about research data online and in-person and who can help colleagues understand specialised or technical concepts, regardless of background or level of technical expertise. You enjoy working in dynamic research environments and are enthusiastic about rapidly acquiring knowledge of new technologies and fields. This role is eligible for hybrid working with a minimum of 20% on site. This appointment is subject to UCL Terms and Conditions of Service for Research and Professional Services Staff. Please visit UCL's HR page for more information. Further information about working in ARC can be found on our website www.ucl.ac.uk/arc If you have any queries regarding the vacancy or application process, please contact Mrs. Jodie Jackson, via e-mail (jodie.jackson@ucl.ac.uk). What we offer The UCL Ways of Working supports colleagues to be successful and happy at UCL through sharing expectations around how we work – please visit www.ucl.ac.uk/ways-of-working to find out more. ​​​​​​​As well as the exciting opportunities this role presents, we also offer some great benefits some of which are below: A yearly promotion scheme across grades. The scheme aims to make it easier for high-performing staff demonstrating the appropriate skills and behaviours of performing at a higher grade to be recognised and to accelerate their internal career progression. 41 Days holiday (27 days annual leave 8 bank holiday and 6 closure days) Additional 5 days’ annual leave purchase scheme Visit https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/reward-and-benefits to find out more Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation, and we want our community to represent the diversity of the world’s talent. We are committed to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to being a place where we all belong. We therefore particularly encourage applications from candidates who are likely to be underrepresented in UCL’s workforce. These include people from Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds; disabled people; LGBTQI+ people; and for our Grade 9 and 10 roles, women. Our department is working towards an Athena SWAN award. We are committed to advancing gender equality within our department. Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: Data Steward - ARC.pdf arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
    },
    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47388&jobTitle=Assistant+Research+Data+Steward": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Data Steward",
      "description": "Job details: Assistant Research Data Steward Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Assistant Research Data Steward Apply Now Ref Number B01-05628 Professional Expertise IT and Digital Department Vice-President (Operations) (B01) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £36,433-£41,833 Contract Type Permanent Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment No Closing Date 13-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About us The UCL Centre for Advanced Research Computing (ARC) is UCL’s new institute for infrastructure and innovation in digital research - the supercomputers, datasets, software and people that make computational science and digital scholarship possible. We are an innovative hybrid: a professional services department that delivers reliable and secure infrastructure and services to UCL research groups, and a laboratory for research and innovation in the application of advanced computational and data intensive research methods, working in partnership with academics from all fields. We are a home for the research technology professionals - research software engineers, HPC systems engineers, dev-ops specialists, data engineers, data scientists and data stewards - who support and collaborate in the delivery of UCL research. About the role Our Research Data Stewards provide data-focused support and consultancy to researchers at UCL, helping researchers to improve their data management, align with university and funder policies, and enable Open Science and FAIR data. Research Data Stewards also perform independent research into the practice of data and compute intensive research methods. They will spend much of their time embedded within research projects but also contribute to new research proposals and collaborate on research data service design, feeding in researcher requirements to ensure that the suite of research support services offered by UCL remains relevant and effective. This is a Hybrid working role. Salary range for the Assistant Research Data Steward: £36,433 to £42,891 (including London Allowance) depending on experience. Job description and person specification for the Assistant Research Data Steward position can be accessed at the bottom of this page. Please supply a cover letter setting out how you meet the selection criteria. About you As a Research Data Steward, you’ll bring knowledge of conducting or supporting data intensive‑research. You will be committed to producing reliable, sustainable and trustworthy research data and will have experience analysing and solving complex problems. We’re looking for someone who enjoys communicating about research data online and in-person and who can help colleagues understand specialised or technical concepts, regardless of background or level of technical expertise. You enjoy working in dynamic research environments and are enthusiastic about rapidly acquiring knowledge of new technologies and fields. This role is eligible for hybrid working with a minimum of 20% on site. This appointment is subject to UCL Terms and Conditions of Service for Research and Professional Services Staff. Please visit UCL's HR page for more information. Further information about working in ARC can be found on our website www.ucl.ac.uk/arc If you have any queries regarding the vacancy or application process, please contact Mrs. Jodie Jackson, via e-mail (jodie.jackson@ucl.ac.uk). What we offer The UCL Ways of Working supports colleagues to be successful and happy at UCL through sharing expectations around how we work – please visit www.ucl.ac.uk/ways-of-working to find out more. ​​​​​​​As well as the exciting opportunities this role presents, we also offer some great benefits some of which are below: A yearly promotion scheme across grades. The scheme aims to make it easier for high-performing staff demonstrating the appropriate skills and behaviours of performing at a higher grade to be recognised and to accelerate their internal career progression. 41 Days holiday (27 days annual leave 8 bank holiday and 6 closure days) Additional 5 days’ annual leave purchase scheme Visit https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/reward-and-benefits to find out more Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation, and we want our community to represent the diversity of the world’s talent. We are committed to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to being a place where we all belong. We therefore particularly encourage applications from candidates who are likely to be underrepresented in UCL’s workforce. These include people from Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds; disabled people; LGBTQI+ people; and for our Grade 9 and 10 roles, women. Our department is working towards an Athena SWAN award. We are committed to advancing gender equality within our department. Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: Data Steward - ARC.pdf arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
