    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47403&jobTitle=Brand+Executive+%28Fixed+Term+Contract%29+-++Internal+Applicants+Only": {
      "title": "Brand Executive (Fixed Term Contract)",
      "description": "Job details: Brand Executive (Fixed Term Contract) -  Internal Applicants Only Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Brand Executive (Fixed Term Contract) -  Internal Applicants Only Apply Now Ref Number B23-00219 Professional Expertise External Engagement, Communications, Marketing and Events Department Vice-President (External Engagement) (B23) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £43,981-£54,019​ Contract Type Fixed-term Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment Yes Closing Date 03-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About us At UCL, we do things differently. Founded in 1826, UCL was the first university in England to welcome students regardless of religion and the first to welcome women to higher education. Today, we are one of the world's leading universities, home to over 50,000 students and 15,000 staff, united by a shared commitment to advancing knowledge and improving lives. The Brand team sits within Vice-President External Engagement, the function responsible for strengthening UCL's reputation, influence and public profile. Together, we deliver communications, marketing and engagement activity that reflects the excellence of our research, education and innovation. As we continue to embed and evolve our brand across a complex and diverse institution, we're looking for a talented Brand Executive to help bring the UCL brand to life in meaningful and consistent ways. About the role This is an exciting opportunity for a brand professional who enjoys combining strategic thinking with hands-on delivery. Working closely with the Head of Brand, you'll support the implementation and governance of UCL's brand narrative, visual identity and tone of voice across the university. You'll partner with colleagues from faculties, professional services teams and external suppliers to ensure brand activity is aligned, impactful and distinctive. From advising stakeholders on brand application and managing brand resources, to supporting communications, digital content, photography and brand projects, you'll play a key role in shaping how UCL presents itself to audiences around the world. You'll also help develop brand tools, maintain digital assets, support reporting and analytics, manage relationships with agencies and suppliers, and champion best practice across the organisation. As a visible ambassador for the brand, you'll contribute to building understanding, confidence and engagement with the UCL brand community. This role offers the opportunity to influence brand experiences at scale while working within one of the most respected and recognisable institutions in higher education. Please note, this is an internal recruitment advert, available to eligible UCL workers only. The role is offered on a fixed term contract/secondment basis until 31st July 2027. The role offered hybrid working with currently a minimum of 2-days per week onsite at our Bidborough House office (subject to change). Job Ref: B23-00221 Closing Date: 03-09-2026 – 23:59 (UK time) About you You'll be a confident and collaborative brand professional with experience delivering successful brand, marketing or communications projects within a complex organisation. Whether your background is in-house, agency-side, higher education or another large-scale environment, you'll understand the importance of balancing creativity with consistency and governance. You will have excellent communication and relationship-building skills, enabling you to work effectively with colleagues, senior stakeholders, external agencies and suppliers. Comfortable advising others and influencing decisions, you'll be able to adapt your approach to different audiences while ensuring communications remain accessible, inclusive and aligned with brand objectives. Highly organised and detail-oriented, you'll enjoy managing multiple priorities and seeing projects through from concept to delivery. You'll bring strong editorial judgement, an eye for visual identity, and a commitment to maintaining high standards across every touchpoint. Most importantly, you'll be curious, proactive and enthusiastic about the power of brand. You'll enjoy working as part of a team, building partnerships across a diverse institution and helping colleagues understand, champion and apply the UCL brand. Experience within higher education would be beneficial, but we're equally interested in candidates who can bring fresh perspectives, ideas and expertise from other sectors. What we offer Standard UCL Benefits: 41 days’ holiday (27 days annual leave, 8 bank holidays, 6 closure days) Option to purchase 5 additional days’ annual leave Defined benefit career average revalued earnings pension scheme (CARE) Cycle to work scheme, season ticket loan, and immigration loan Relocation support for eligible posts On-site nursery and gym Enhanced maternity, paternity, and adoption pay Staff Support Service (employee assistance programme) Discounted medical insurance Full details: UCL Rewards and Benefits . Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation. We are committed to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to being a place where we all belong. We particularly encourage applications from candidates underrepresented in UCL’s workforce, including those from Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds, disabled people, and – for Grade 9 and 10 roles – women. Read more: UCL Equality, Diversity and Inclusion . Applicants should also familiarise themselves with UCL’s policies on: Prevention of Bullying, Harassment and Sexual Misconduct Policy and Personal Relationships Policy Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: Brand Executive August 2026.docx arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
