    "https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/search-ucl-jobs/details?jobId=47784&jobTitle=Casework+and+Student+Support+Manager": {
      "title": "Casework and Student Support Manager",
      "description": "Job details: Casework and Student Support Manager Skip to job title Skip to action buttons Close Study Research Engage About Give Work at UCL Home Home Search Jobs Application Process Rewards and Benefits Careers Community People Around UCL Temporary Work UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details UCL Home Work at UCL Search UCL Jobs Job details Casework and Student Support Manager Apply Now Ref Number B04-07753 Professional Expertise Administration and Business Support Department UCL BEAMS (B04) Location London Working Pattern Full time Salary £56,431-£66,437​ Contract Type Permanent Working Type Hybrid Available for Secondment No Closing Date 16-Sept-2026 JD_Param11 Yes JD_Param12 Yes About Us The UCL Faculty of Mathematical and Physical Sciences (MAPS) is comprised of eight departments that are highly rated for research excellence: Chemistry; Physics & Astronomy; Space & Climate Physics; Mathematics; Science & Technology Studies; Earth Sciences; Risk and Disaster Reduction and Statistical Science. In addition, the faculty has its own interdepartmental undergraduate degree programme: Natural Sciences. UCL Mathematical and Physical Sciences employs over 1,400 members of staff, of whom approximately 80% are academic, teaching and research staff and 20% professional services.  There are approximately 4430 undergraduate students, 950 postgraduate taught students and 1060 postgraduate research students.  The faculty prides itself on providing a rich and culturally diverse environment for students and staff alike. About the role The purpose of this role is to provide Faculty level leadership and management of student casework, support, success and welfare related activity. Leading the faculty’s Student Support and Success team, they will oversee the coordination of student casework that requires faculty approval or intervention and support programmes and departments in MAPS dealing with individual casework, student support procedures and student welfare. The role will lead on Faculty-level student success initiatives, support inclusive, data-informed approaches to education in alignment with UCL’s Education Strategy and EDI objectives. They will work closely with the Vice-Dean (Education), Faculty Student Success Lead and other colleagues to embed equitable practices across the curriculum and co-curricular activities. The role will oversee projects related to awarding gaps and student engagement, driving innovation and acting as a key liaison with UCL’s student success networks. The post is available from 1 October 2026. Please explain how you meet the essential and desirable criteria, which are mentioned in the job description, in the \"Statement in support of your application\" section. About you The role holder must have experience of overseeing or coordinating student support processes, leading or overseeing student casework or comparable regulated experiences including decision making and management of procedures and risk and experience of a management role.  In addition, excellent communication, interpersonal and leadership skills, good knowledge of policy and best practice around access and participation, and commitment to advancing equality, diversity and inclusion are essential attributes for this role. What we offer As well as the exciting opportunities this role presents, we also offer great benefits. Please visit https://www.ucl.ac.uk/work-at-ucl/rewards-and-benefits to find out more. A job description and person specification can be accessed at the bottom of this page. If you have any queries about the role, please contact Sophie Malin ( s.malin@ucl.ac.uk ). Our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion As London’s Global University, we know diversity fosters creativity and innovation, and we want our community to represent the diversity of the world’s talent. We are committed to equality of opportunity, to being fair and inclusive, and to being a place where we all belong. We therefore particularly encourage applications from candidates who are likely to be underrepresented in UCL’s workforce. These include people from Black, Asian and ethnic minority backgrounds; disabled people; LGBTQI+ people; and for our Grade 9 and 10 roles, women. You can read more about our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion here: https://www.ucl.ac.uk/equality-diversity-inclusion/ Available documents Attached documents are available under links. Clicking a document link will initialize its download. download: MAPS Grade 8 Casework and Student Support Manager.pdf arrow_back Back to list Send job to a friend Print this page Apply Now Apply Now Information for Current students Staff Alumni Business Donors Visit Maps Library, museums and collections Bloomsbury Theatre UCL East Tours and visits Connect with UCL Jobs Media Relations Events UCL and London UCL Shop University College London, Gower Street, London, WC1E 6BT Tel: +44 (0) 20 7679 2000 Copyright © 2026 UCL Disclaimer Freedom of Information Accessibility Privacy and Cookies Slavery statement Contact Us Privacy & Cookie Settings We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyse site traffic, and serve personalised content. You can manage your preferences at any time. Accept all cookies Accept necessary cookies Settings Privacy Policy : Learn more about how we handle your data and protect your privacy. UCL privacy policy Privacy Preferences Configure your privacy preferences for different types of cookies and tracking technologies. Necessary Essential for the website to function properly. These cannot be disabled. Learn more These cookies are required for: • User authentication and secure login • Maintaining your session while browsing • Processing secure payments • Preventing security threats and fraud • Remembering items in your shopping cart Analytics Help us improve by understanding visitor behaviour. Learn more We use analytics to: • Understand which pages are most popular • Monitor site performance and loading times • Track visitor journeys and navigation patterns • Identify technical issues and errors • Measure the effectiveness of our content Common providers: Google Analytics, Matomo, Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity Marketing Deliver relevant ads and measure campaigns. Learn more Marketing cookies help us: • Show you relevant advertisements • Measure ad campaign effectiveness • Limit how often you see the same ad • Understand your interests and preferences • Track conversions from advertising Common providers: Google Ads, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, Twitter Ads, Amazon Advertising Embeds Enable third-party content and features. Learn more Important: These third-party services may set their own cookies that we cannot control. Types of embedded content: • YouTube and Vimeo videos • Social media posts and feeds • Microsoft Forms and surveys • Interactive maps and location services • Live chat and support widgets • External booking systems Save Preferences"
